' ==Access Granting Flow (FHIR R4 Consent Standard)==
' Patient -> App : Grant access to Dr (search by doctor ID)
' App -> nginx : access grant creation req\n{doctorId, scopes[], resourceTypes[], purpose[], expiresIn}
' nginx -> NJS : forward request with patient's access token

' NJS -> NJS : validate patient token & extract patientId
' NJS -> FHIR : Verify patient owns their data (GET /Patient/{patientId})
' FHIR -> NJS : Patient resource confirmed

' NJS -> NJS : Validate requested scopes/purposes against patient's rights

' NJS -> App : Request patient verification\n(e.g., 2FA, PIN, biometric)
' App -> Patient : Display Consent Form
' Patient -> App : Confirm 
' App -> NJS : Verification confirmed

' NJS -> FHIR : Create Consent resource (FHIR R4)\n{\n  status: "active",\n  grantor: Patient,\n  grantee: Practitioner/doctorId,\n  decision: "permit",\n  provision: {\n    actor: doctorId,\n    purpose: ["TREAT"],\n    resourceType: ["Condition","Encounter"],\n    period: {start, end}\n  },\n  verification: {\n    verified: true,\n    verificationType: "Patient signature",\n    verificationDate: now\n  }\n}
' FHIR -> NJS : Consent resource created with consentId

' ' access:grant:{patientId}:{doctorId}\nValue: {grantId, scopes, expiresAt}\nTTL: patient-specified duration
' ' grantId : specific value for currently active session

==Access Granting Flow==
Doctor -> Browser : search for patient (by id)
Browser->nginx: Request access to patient data using PID
nginx->NJS : forward request 
' with Dr's access token
NJS-> TDB : Retrieve PID token
TDB-> NJS : return patient token
NJS->Firebase: Push notifictaion req 
note left of NJS : req includes relevant details (dr id , timestamp, title , etc..)
Firebase-> Application : send req


alt patient approves

Application-> NJS : Forward Approval
 NJS -> App : Request patient verification
 note left of NJS:(e.g 2FA, PIN, biometric)
App -> Patient : Display Consent Form
Patient -> App : Confirm 
App -> NJS : Verification
NJS -> NJS : generate grant signature 
note right of NJS: (HMAC of consentId+scope+expiry)
NJS -> ADB : Store grant 
ADB -> NJS : Grant stored
NJS -> AR : Cache access grant for fast lookup Key
note left of NJS: access grant:{PID}:{doctorID} Value: {consentId, scopes, expiresAt, signature}\nTTL: patient-specified dur.
AR -> NJS : Grant cached successfully

note right of NJS : create database for consent storage? , database/redis for mobile token?
else patient refuses

Application->Application : do nothing 
note right of Application : (avoid alerting dr, best sec practice)

end

note left of Patient: "Patient login (&& notif permission granted) -> app Gets token from firebase , sends to backend , backend stores  token associated to PID to send notifictaions later"

